# Hand labels for synth.rs, written with the file (bench, relight 174). The decisions this fixture pins:
#   a ghost field is SPEC (model state) · a type_invariant spec fn is SPEC · an exec fn's requires/ensures lines are SPEC
#   (the clause keyword lines and their continuations) · an exec fn's `decreases` is PROOF · a multi-line assert ... by { }
#   is PROOF through its close · a proof fn is PROOF in whole, its requires/ensures included (a lemma's statement is proof
#   scaffolding, not the component's spec) · a brace in a string is not a brace · a line with code and a trailing comment is
#   code · line 24's string carries an unbalanced { and ( so the string-blanking arm can fail (a balanced one could
#   not: found by mutant, relight 174) · `#[cfg(test)] mod` in solution.rs is TEST · the `verus! {` opener and its close are IMPL (structure).
# Hand totals: SPEC 10 · PROOF 12 · IMPL 21 · TEST 5 · COMMENT 2 · BLANK 7 = 57.
# Line 49 `assert!(a < 100);` is a Rust runtime assertion, IMPL (added relight 174 after the population read 11 plain
# cells with PROOF > 0: the statement rule matched `assert!`).
